    {
      "name": "Screenshot",
      "description": "Captures a fast screenshot-first desktop snapshot with cursor position, desktop/window summaries, and an image. This path skips UI tree extraction for speed. Use Snapshot when you need interactive element ids, scrollable regions, or browser DOM extraction. Set display=[0] or display=[0,1] using zero-based active Windows display indices to capture only those monitors. Set region=[left, top, right, bottom] in virtual-desktop pixel coordinates to capture only that rectangle instead of the whole screen/display \u2014 useful when you already know which area matters and want to save tokens; region takes precedence over display when both are given, and an invalid or out-of-bounds region raises an error rather than silently capturing something else. Note: the returned image may be downscaled for efficiency; when it is, multiply image coordinates by the ratio of original size to displayed size to get the actual screen coordinates for mouse actions (Click, Move, etc.).",
      "inputSchema": {
        "type": "object",
        "additionalProperties": false,
        "properties": {
          "use_annotation": {
